From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: run without an IOMMU (the VRAM carveout)

msm falls back to its VRAM carveout when the GPU has no IOMMU
(msm_iommu_new() returns NULL for a device that is not iommu-mapped,
msm_gpu_init() prints "no IOMMU, fallback to VRAM carveout!" and leaves
gpu->aspace NULL): msm_gem_new() then allocates every object from the
carveout with a VMA of no address space whose iova is the physical
address, and pinning such an object maps nothing (msm_gem_vma_map()
returns early without an address space). Of the a6xx code, two places
dereference the address space unconditionally:

- a6xx_create_private_address_space() calls
  msm_iommu_pagetable_create(gpu->aspace->mmu) at every DRM open
  (context_init -> msm_gpu_create_private_address_space). It now returns
  -ENODEV without gpu->aspace; an error rather than NULL, since its caller
  only falls back to the global address space for IS_ERR_OR_NULL and
  writes aspace->pid for anything that is not an error.
- a6xx_set_pagetable() reads ctx->aspace->mmu at every submit; without an
  address space there is no page table to switch to.

msm.ko on FreeBSD (freebsd/gpu/msm-port.md, decision A) runs the SM6115's
Adreno 610 like this, its SMMU in bypass.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -113,6 +113,13 @@
 	if (ctx->seqno == a6xx_gpu->base.base.cur_ctx_seqno)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Without an IOMMU (the VRAM carveout, gpu->aspace NULL) there are no
+	 * per-process pagetables to switch to
+	 */
+	if (!ctx->aspace)
+		return;
+
 	if (msm_iommu_pagetable_params(ctx->aspace->mmu, &ttbr, &asid))
 		return;
 
@@ -2058,6 +2065,14 @@
 {
 	struct msm_mmu *mmu;
 
+	/*
+	 * No IOMMU (the VRAM carveout): no private address spaces; an error,
+	 * not NULL, so that msm_gpu_create_private_address_space() falls
+	 * back to gpu->aspace
+	 */
+	if (!gpu->aspace)
+		return ERR_PTR(-ENODEV);
+
 	mmu = msm_iommu_pagetable_create(gpu->aspace->mmu);
 
 	if (IS_ERR(mmu))
